From fe2fb71b64a7e8de19ee4be3f0d4bfbd28c23dfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jordan Williams Johnson <jordandwj@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:24:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] etnaviv/ml: CPU access to compiled 1x1 coefficients (LLM
 engine, test tree only)

etna_ml_llm_coefs() (new header etnaviv_ml_llm.h) returns the i-th NN
job's coefficient BO, CPU-mapped, with the V7 pointwise layout it was
written in (cores, header size, kernels per core, superblocks, block
stride, zero point). etna_ml_create_coeffs_v7() records that layout;
ETNA_ML_CACHED_COEFFS=1 allocates the coefficient BOs CPU-cached
instead of write-combined so the CPU can read them at full speed.

The LLM engine uses it to run one-token decode on the CPU straight from
the NPU's weight buffers, with no second copy of the weights: on the
A311D, SmolLM2-1.7B decodes at 340 ms per token from these buffers,
bit-identical to decoding from the original rows (alta-npu
runs/llm-prefill5-ladder-20261124-034056).

Unset = unchanged: fake-NPU submits byte-identical.

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
